{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\n#include <tuple>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nint main() {\n    i64 x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n    i64 best_a = 0, best_b = 1;\n    i64 best_score = LLONG_MAX;\n\n    for (i64 b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n        i64 a0 = (x * b) / y;\n        for (i64 a = max(a0 - 10, 0LL); a <= a0 + 9; ++a) {\n            i64 diff = llabs(x * b - a * y);\n            i64 score = diff * best_b;\n            i64 current = best_score * b;\n            \n            if (score < current || \n                (score == current && \n                 (b < best_b || (b == best_b && a < best_a)))) {\n                best_score = score;\n                best_a = a;\n                best_b = b;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << best_a << \"/\" << best_b << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef main():\n    x, y, n = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().s